## Code Standards

---

### Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Classes | `PascalCase` | `Content_Analyzer` |
| Methods | `snake_case()` | `get_post_meta()` |
| Properties | `$snake_case` | `$post_id` |
| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `SE_VERSION` |
| Files | Match class name | `Content_Analyzer.php` |

PHP Namespace: `SiteEssentials\`
One class per file. File name must match class name.

For meta key and option naming conventions, see: `.cursor/rules/meta-key-prefixes.mdc`

---

### Hook Registration — Always Use Named Callbacks

```php
// ✅ Named class method — can be removed later
add_action( 'save_post', [ $this, 'on_save_post' ], 10, 3 );
add_action( 'init', [ self::class, 'register_post_type' ] );

// ❌ Anonymous function — cannot be removed, do not use
add_action( 'init', function() {
    // This hook can never be unregistered
} );
```

**Hook priorities:**
- Default (10) unless there is a specific reason to change it
- If using a non-default priority, add a comment explaining why

---

### Database Queries — Use WP Methods, Not Direct SQL

```php
// ✅ Use get_posts() or WP_Query
$posts = get_posts( [
    'post_type'      => 'post',
    'posts_per_page' => 10,
    'no_found_rows'  => true, // Skip COUNT query when pagination not needed
] );

// ❌ Avoid direct SQL unless absolutely necessary
$posts = $wpdb->get_results( "SELECT * FROM {$wpdb->posts} WHERE post_type = 'post'" );
```

---

### Post Meta — Always Batch-Load

When looping over multiple posts, pre-load meta in a single query. Never load meta individually inside a loop.

```php
// ✅ Batch-load: 1 query for all meta
$post_ids = wp_list_pluck( $posts, 'ID' );
update_meta_cache( 'post', $post_ids );

foreach ( $posts as $post ) {
    $value = get_post_meta( $post->ID, 'scos_seo_metatitle', true ); // From cache
}

// ❌ N+1 queries — one per post
foreach ( $posts as $post ) {
    $value = get_post_meta( $post->ID, 'scos_seo_metatitle', true ); // Hits DB every time
}
```

