### Performance Benchmarks

These are the targets — flag any code that risks exceeding them:

| Metric | Limit |
|--------|-------|
| Admin page load | < 500ms |
| Frontend overhead | < 50ms |
| Additional queries per page | < 5 |
| Memory increase | < 10MB |

Use `Cache_Helper::remember()` for any expensive or repeated operations:

```php
$data = Cache_Helper::remember( 'unique_cache_key', function() {
    return expensive_database_query();
}, 3600, 'module_name' ); // TTL in seconds, grouped by module
```

Invalidate cache on data change:

```php
add_action( 'save_post', function( $post_id ) {
    Cache_Helper::flush( 'module_name' );
} );
```

---

### Module Interface

Every module must implement `Module_Interface`. Required methods:

```php
// Static — module metadata
public static function get_id();
public static function get_name();
public static function get_description();
public static function get_tier();           // basic | pro | agency
public static function get_dependencies();   // array of module IDs
public static function get_version();

// Instance — lifecycle
public function init();
public function render_settings();
```

Module directory structure:
```
modules/
└── {module-name}/
    ├── {Module_Name}_Module.php
    ├── class-{feature}.php
    ├── views/
    │   └── settings.php
    └── assets/
        ├── css/
        └── js/
```
